{
  "id": "tr808-fischer",
  "name": "TR-808 Recordings",
  "tagline": "808 recordings by Michael Fischer (1994), CC0",
  "description": "116 one-shots recorded directly from a real Roland TR-808 (serial no. 103852) by Michael Fischer of Technopolis in 1994: 25 bass drums and 25 snares across the tone/decay and tone/snappy knobs, 25 cymbals, toms, congas, open hats and every other voice, each from its individual output at 16-bit/44.1 kHz. The '808 Classic' kit puts all 16 instruments on the pads; '808 Boom' keeps the essentials on bank A and plays the long-decay bass drum as a tuned 808 bass on bank B (C minor scale, pads choke each other). File names follow the original knob positions, e.g. bd0010 = tone 0, decay 10 (see README.md).",
  "tags": [
    "808",
    "drum machine",
    "analog",
    "hip-hop",
    "trap",
    "electro"
  ],
  "author": "Michael Fischer (Technopolis)",
